<section class="inner-page-heading" id="inspections">

      <div class="services-inline-3 container">

        <p class="eyebrow">Professor Jerry RV Inspections</p>

        <h1>RV Inspections</h1>

        <p class="lead">RV Inspections Information and Pricing</p>

      </div>

    </section>



    <section class="section">

      <div class="container inner-page-content">

        <p>

          An RV is a major purchase. Just as you'd have a home inspected before buying it,

          you can have an independent inspector look over the RV before you sign. That

          applies whether you're buying a used RV or taking delivery of a

          brand-new RV.

        </p>



        <p>

          On a used RV, the inspection can help you spot wear, damage, or systems that

          aren't working as expected. On a new RV, it gives you a chance to bring issues

          to the dealer's attention before delivery. A warranty can help cover eligible

          repairs, but you may still have to wait for a service appointment.

        </p>



        <h3 id="certified-inspector">Why Choose a Certified RV Inspector?</h3>

        <p>

          An RV packs a lot into a small space. It has plumbing, propane, batteries,

          120-volt electrical circuits, appliances, heating and cooling, and often

          slide-outs or leveling equipment. A system can appear to work during a quick

          walkthrough and still perform poorly when tested.

        </p>



        <p>

          A certified RV inspector is trained to check those systems methodically and

          document what they find. I use inspection software designed for RVs to record

          the condition of the roof, exterior, and accessible systems. The result is a

          written record you can refer to when deciding what to ask the seller about

          before you buy.

        </p>



        <!-- Original wording
<p>I am certified through the <b>National RV Inspectors Association (<a target="_new"

              href="https://nrvia.org">NRVIA)</a></b> which enforce vigorous

          education, requirements, and code of ethics for its members.




-->
        <p>I am a Certified RV Inspector through the <a href="https://nrvia.org" target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">National RV Inspectors Association (NRVIA)</a>. My work reflects the training and
          professional standards associated with that certification.</p>

        <h3 id="inspection-process">What Happens During an Inspection?</h3>

        <p>

          Plan on about five to ten hours on site, depending on the RV's size and

          features. The on-site inspection takes place in a single calendar day. I take

          hundreds of photos and select the ones that best show the RV's condition and

          the findings that matter. A detailed report may run 100 pages or more and

          include around 80 to 100 photos.

        </p>



        <p>

          The report lists the most serious findings first, including any life safety

          concerns. If a finding raises a safety concern, I may recommend having a

          qualified RV technician evaluate it before you enter, drive, or move the RV.

        </p>



        <p>

          The inspection documents observed conditions and potential problems. A

          qualified technician can use those findings to diagnose the cause and

          recommend repairs. For motorhomes, the inspection covers the RV portion.

          Arrange a separate mechanical inspection if you want the engine evaluated.

        </p>

        <section>

          <h3 id="inspection-types">Types of Inspections</h3>

          <p>We offer two types of inspections for each class/size of RV.</p>


          <div style="width:100%">
            <div class="about-portrait">
              <img src="/assets/images/essentials.png" alt="Essentials" loading="lazy">
            </div>
            <p>The Essentials Inspection focuses on the inspection categories you select. Pricing depends on the scope
              of work. You receive a PDF report documenting the areas inspected and identifying it as a limited-scope
              Essentials Inspection. Contact me for an estimate tailored to your RV and your needs.</p>
          </div>


          <div style="width:100%; clear:both">
            <div class="about-portrait">
              <img src="/assets/images/completecertified.png" alt="Complete Certified" loading="lazy">
            </div>
            <p>The Complete Certified Inspection provides a comprehensive review of your RV&rsquo;s accessible areas and
              systems within the inspection&rsquo;s scope. You receive a detailed PDF report documenting the findings
              for your records and discussions with the seller.</p>
        </section>

